# Claude edit blocklist — one pattern per line.
# Enforced by .claude/edit-guard.mjs via a PreToolUse hook on Edit|Write|MultiEdit.
#
# This is what makes "human-owned" real rather than aspirational: a skill told
# not to edit a file will mostly comply, but a hook always does. Put every doc
# whose authority is the human's here — specs, requirement sources, raw idea
# dumps — plus the guard's own files, so a session cannot disarm it.
#
# Syntax:
#   docs/              — block an entire folder
#   docs/SPEC.md       — exact relative path
#   *.lock             — glob on filename
#   src/generated/**   — glob on full path
#
# NOTE: patterns also match on basename alone, so a bare `edit-blocklist` blocks
# any file with that name anywhere — including in other checkouts. Prefer
# path-qualified patterns for project files.

# --- the guard itself (do not remove) ---
.claude/edit-blocklist
.claude/edit-guard.mjs

# --- human-owned sources of truth: EDIT THIS SECTION FOR YOUR PROJECT ---
# The spec / requirements doc(s) that define correctness. Claude proposes diffs
# to these; only you apply them.
docs/SPEC.md

# The raw, unmaintained idea dump /triage reads from. Read-only by design: it is
# explicitly *not* a source of truth, and letting a skill "tidy" it destroys the
# provenance that makes it useful.
docs/dev_notes/

# Vendored third-party docs, if any — never ours to edit.
# docs/vendor/
